  {
    "index": 3,
    "hash": "2B+a0P0UBPr//cAHt5cL0CGtsb8=",
    "timestampUtcMs": "2026-08-14T12:35:55.000Z",
    "action": {
      "type": "SET_CONTENT",
      "input": {
        "content": "`subscribeToSource(source, callback)` is the change-notification half of `IAnalyticsStore`. It returns an unsubscribe function rather than taking a handle, so cleanup is a closure:\n\n```typescript\nconst unsub = store.subscribeToSource(\n  AnalyticsPath.fromString(\"atlas/\"),\n  (source) => { /* decide whether to requery */ },\n);\n// later\nunsub();\n```\n\nMatching follows the same path semantics as the rest of the engine. Given a subscription to `atlas/`:\n\n- `atlas/foo` fires it\n- `atlas/foo/bar` fires it\n- `rwa/foo` does not\n\nWildcards work at interior segments too. `atlas/*/test` fires for `atlas/foo/test`, `atlas/another-thing/test`, and `atlas/foo/test/a/b/c` \u2014 but not `rwa/foo/test`.\n\nThe mechanics in `AnalyticsSubscriptionManager` are worth knowing because they explain a surprise: notification walks the *prefixes of the updated path* and matches them against registered subscriptions. So an update to `/a/b/c` notifies subscribers of `/a/b/c`, `/a/b`, and `/a`. Wildcard patterns are then checked separately, segment by segment, and a wildcard subscription longer than the update path cannot match. Callbacks are wrapped in try/catch and every subscriber is delivered to even if an earlier one throws; the collected errors are re-raised together as a `NotificationError` after delivery completes.\n\nThe callback receives the updated `AnalyticsPath`, not the data. It is a hint to requery, which is exactly how `useAnalyticsQuery`'s `sources` option turns a static query into a live one.\n\nProvenance: draft `03-Build/04-WorkWithData/_06-Analytics Engine/typescript/index.md`; behaviour verified in `packages/analytics-engine/core/src/AnalyticsSubscriptionManager.ts` and the interface in `packages/shared/analytics/types.ts` at 6.2.2-dev.45.",
        "updatedAt": "2026-08-14T12:35:55.000Z"
      },
      "timestampUtcMs": "2026-08-14T12:35:55.000Z"
    }
  },
